Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Topology", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The topology of a substrate is read off its metric balls. The closed balls \
of one radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "650dd49b-e1ff-4d2d-9811-5092f44eee49"],
 " generate a topology: a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1adf26fd-f0e2-4b84-b771-e663c6d1bde5"],
 " lies in the closure of a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "152a0fd5-dd44-4c6f-86bc-758f941ea6cf"],
 " when the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6698285-ae10-4c3c-a3b9-5de2d92dec40"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "540bd9c2-2212-403e-a0d0-d1de47b0d929"],
 " is contained in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aed5cc9-93ff-43d1-8d5e-cb9492689220"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55fde4f3-d7e4-4913-ba06-9ac8197e702a"],
 ". This specialization preorder carries closure, interior, boundary, \
neighbourhood and continuity. A family of balls forms a complex through its \
intersections: a simplex is admitted when every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "508158d6-5663-4886-a423-80471ff69746"],
 " of its balls have a common point, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5920c953-f322-4eac-90f8-a491f63232fd"],
 " gives the Vietoris-Rips complex of twice the radius, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46fe92cd-6890-4726-ac41-d7f558a78e3e"],
 " the Cech complex, and the orders between interpolate. The least number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe660ae2-528b-4a09-9f4a-f55102e88e51"],
 " of balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5df1c02-14e7-4779-b5a3-cee37ffd54a1"],
 " that cover the substrate falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3851de04-181e-41b8-bc41-2f2f06995199"],
 " grows, and the rate of that fall is a dimension."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

